WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.553
"You had a Red Share with Gliss?" Perda sounded surprised.

2
00:00:04.554 --> 00:00:07.359
"I didn't know you two were so close."

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.884
"Me neither," Darb said quietly.

4
00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:13.318
Zann didn't say anything. He was surprised himself.

5
00:00:13.319 --> 00:00:18.229
Usually Red Shares only happened between family members or very close friends.

6
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:23.428
"Gliss is the girl who was captured this morning, yes?" Teplo said thoughtfully.

7
00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:28.932
"It's interesting that you received the Share now rather than when the trolls grabbed her."

8
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:33.670
Perda nodded. "I'm sure Gliss has been terrified ever since she was taken.

9
00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:36.896
The Share means something just scared her even more."

10
00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:42.275
Teplo yanked the rope again. "Where is Fala?" he exclaimed.

11
00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:47.247
A door opened in the back of the room. "Sorry," Fala said breathlessly.

12
00:00:47.248 --> 00:00:51.206
"I was distracted, watching the trolls on the Remote Eye."

13
00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:54.131
"What's a Remote Eye?" Perda asked.

14
00:00:54.132 --> 00:00:59.605
Fala glanced at her. "Hey, you're the kids who knocked on the door. How'd you get down here?"

15
00:00:59.606 --> 00:01:01.826
She shot a suspicious look at Teplo.

16
00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:07.099
"Did you use the trapdoor? I told you—that thing's dangerous!"

17
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.186
Teplo grinned sheepishly. "I put cushions under the hole."

18
00:01:11.187 --> 00:01:16.603
Fala rolled her eyes. "Sorry about that," she told the kids.

19
00:01:16.604 --> 00:01:20.307
Then she noticed that Darb was gnawing on a turnip cookie.

20
00:01:20.308 --> 00:01:24.380
"Are you hungry? You don't have to eat those disgusting things."

21
00:01:24.381 --> 00:01:29.664
"Disgusting?" Teplo said. "Turnips are extremely nutritious!"

22
00:01:29.665 --> 00:01:34.126
Ignoring him, Fala conjured some food and a pitcher of airberry juice.

23
00:01:34.128 --> 00:01:39.174
"Thank you!" Perda exclaimed. "We can't use magic right now."

24
00:01:39.175 --> 00:01:42.948
"I know he can't." Fala pointed at Zann.

25
00:01:42.949 --> 00:01:46.792
"But as far as we know, the trolls are only targeting Reds."

26
00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:51.410
"That's what I thought," Teplo said. "But wait until you hear their story!"

27
00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.384
He told Fala what the kids had just told him.

28
00:01:54.385 --> 00:01:57.348
"That's quite a tale," she said when he was finished.

29
00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:00.478
"I think I saw Gliss on the Remote Eye this morning.

30
00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:02.968
She's a pretty girl about your age, right?"

31
00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:10.108
Zann realized that Fala had never answered Perda's question. "What's a Remote Eye?" he asked.

32
00:02:10.109 --> 00:02:16.148
"It's an ancient type of magic, long forgotten in these peaceful times," Teplo said.

33
00:02:16.149 --> 00:02:22.341
"It's a way to watch someone without being seen—and without using a spy fly."

34
00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:31.064
Fala nodded. "In the Old Times, Magicians often created devices that focused their energy through certain arrangements of special objects.

35
00:02:31.065 --> 00:02:37.942
Some of the plans still exist, though these ancient texts are only available to advanced scholars at the university."

36
00:02:37.943 --> 00:02:44.768
"Why?" Perda asked. "If these old devices make better magic, shouldn't everyone know about them?"

37
00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:51.399
"It's not that simple," replied Teplo. "The devices often had unintended side effects.

38
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.936
Besides, many devices required components that are unlawful or immoral to possess today."

39
00:02:57.937 --> 00:03:00.555
"Like what?" said Zann.

40
00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:08.423
Teplo looked uneasy. "Well, for instance, a Remote Eye was originally supposed to contain an actual eye."

41
00:03:08.424 --> 00:03:12.272
"You mean a person's eye?" Darb sounded horrified.

42
00:03:12.273 --> 00:03:19.212
"Ideally, yes," Teplo said. "Though some books suggested using the eye of a dragon instead."

43
00:03:19.213 --> 00:03:25.644
"Is that what you used?" Zann exclaimed, thinking of Zing. "A dragon's eye?"

44
00:03:25.645 --> 00:03:33.296
"Of course not!" Fala said. "We've been experimenting with alternatives, and we finally found one that works.

45
00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:36.816
It's a telescope lens that I borrowed from a Void friend."

46
00:03:36.817 --> 00:03:39.509
"What's a telescope?" Perda asked.

47
00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.905
"It helps you see stuff that's far away," Darb told her.

48
00:03:42.906 --> 00:03:45.916
"It works sort of like a Sight Enhancing spell."

49
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:53.850
"Now if only we could concoct an eardrum substitute, we might be able to hear the trolls as well as see them," Teplo said.

50
00:03:53.851 --> 00:03:58.417
"Meanwhile, Fala, is there any news from our contacts at the palace?"

51
00:03:58.418 --> 00:04:05.272
"A little." Fala looked worried. "The king's assistant just volunteered to take over as king."

52
00:04:05.273 --> 00:04:10.197
"You mean that sneaky little fellow, Slib?" Teplo rolled his eyes.

53
00:04:10.198 --> 00:04:14.167
"He's not fit to rule his own house, let alone Magica."

54
00:04:14.168 --> 00:04:17.953
"He claims the era of Reds is over," Fala said.

55
00:04:17.954 --> 00:04:25.596
"The Red Council—that is, what's left of it—can't do much to prevent him from grabbing power, since the members are all in hiding."

56
00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:29.605
"Well, I'll let the others worry about that." Teplo shrugged.

57
00:04:29.606 --> 00:04:35.874
"I don't care about politics. What I do care about is helping the trolls' prisoners."

58
00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:39.889
Zann nodded. "We have to figure out how to save Gliss.

59
00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.590
Let's go scout out that dragon pen."

60
00:04:42.591 --> 00:04:47.171
"Out of the question," Teplo said. "It's far too dangerous."

61
00:04:47.172 --> 00:04:52.818
"But she's only there because of me," Zann insisted. "I have to save her!"

62
00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:55.598
The others all tried to change his mind.

63
00:04:55.599 --> 00:05:02.087
But Zann was determined, arguing against whatever they said. Finally Teplo sighed.

64
00:05:02.088 --> 00:05:06.177
"He's just as stubborn as his grandfather," he muttered.

65
00:05:06.178 --> 00:05:09.788
"Go if you must, Zann. But you'll need a disguise."

66
00:05:09.789 --> 00:05:12.818
"If he's going, I'll go too," Perda said.

67
00:05:12.819 --> 00:05:17.105
"No," Teplo said. "It's safer if Zann goes alone."

68
00:05:17.106 --> 00:05:21.683
"He's right," Zann said. "You and Darb should stay here."

69
00:05:21.684 --> 00:05:27.584
Teplo glanced at Fala. "Please send a message to the other Reds who remain free.

70
00:05:27.585 --> 00:05:31.442
Maybe they can help keep an eye on Zann in case he gets in trouble."

71
00:05:31.443 --> 00:05:38.606
He sounded doubtful, but Fala nodded and summoned several message moths.

72
00:05:38.607 --> 00:05:42.297
Then she went to work on Zann's disguise.

73
00:05:42.298 --> 00:05:47.389
Teplo tried to convince her to turn Zann's hair purple, but she made it brown instead.

74
00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:52.370
She also hid Zann's freckles with an Illusion spell.

75
00:05:52.371 --> 00:05:55.711
The streets were deserted when Zann left Teplo's house.

76
00:05:55.712 --> 00:06:02.006
The zoo was a dozen blocks away. While he walked, Zann tried to come up with a plan to free Gliss.

77
00:06:02.007 --> 00:06:05.745
How could he defeat Morb's trolls without using magic?

78
00:06:05.746 --> 00:06:08.623
Zann was still thinking as he rounded a corner.

79
00:06:08.624 --> 00:06:11.211
Suddenly he heard a rustle of movement.

80
00:06:11.212 --> 00:06:16.891
But before he could react, he found himself trapped in a dark, floating bubble!

81
00:06:16.892 --> 00:06:19.384
"What's going on?" he cried.

82
00:06:19.385 --> 00:06:29.204
"We know that you're a Red," said a low voice. "You'll need to come with us."

